  "title": "Computation is not a basic physical property",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "93501ef9-00c3-4c81-bbc7-161e4fce2a65",
      "text": "Computation is not a basic physical property of a system: calling a system a computation depends on a description or a purpose brought to it. The frameworks that say so put it differently: a computation names no present physical property its different hardware shares, or computation is execution with a goal that someone sets.",
